        "original_id": "b3562959-fd3c-5788-b0c2-6f11b5e7d5ca",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Felipe Calderón\n- Projects: La Yesca Dam, El Cajón Dam\n- Places: La Yesca, Grande de Santiago River, Barranca de Oblatos, Jalisco, Mexico\n- Topics: Mexican presidency, hydroelectric development\n\nFacts:\n- Felipe Calderón was born on 18 August 1962.\n- El Cajón Dam was completed downstream on the Grande de Santiago River in 2007.\n- Felipe Calderón served as President of Mexico from 1 December 2006 to 30 November 2012.\n- La Yesca Dam on the Grande de Santiago River at La Yesca was completed in 2012.\n- President Felipe Calderón inaugurated La Yesca Dam on 6 November 2012.\n- Barranca de Oblatos, also known as Barranca de Huentitán, is a canyon in Jalisco, Mexico, carved by the Río Grande de Santiago.",
